EXAMPLE CONTENT NOTICE:

The MIT License above applies to the engine (`index.html`, `template/`,
`scripts/`) and to the blanked starter files in `_template/`. It does not
extend to the fictional "Penguin Embeddings" demo paper shipped in
`content/`, `authors.yaml`, `citation.bib`, and `assets/` — that content
exists only to demonstrate the template and is replaced automatically when
you run `python3 scripts/setup.py`.

HOW TO USE THIS TEMPLATE:

1. Use the "Use this template" button on GitHub to create your own repo.
2. Run `python3 scripts/setup.py` to replace the demo paper with blank
   starter files.
3. Edit `project.yaml`, `authors.yaml`, `citation.bib`, and `content/` with
   your own paper's content.
4. Keep this LICENSE file — the engine code stays MIT either way.
